no adjacent W2 in hand. W1 is a terminal, which might be riskier if opponents are collecting terminals, but discards show mixed. W3 is a middle tile, possibly safer. However, looking at history, many honor tiles (J1, J2, J3, F3, F4) have been played, so non-honor tiles might be safer. T7 is a middle tile with some potential but limited by T9 scarcity. B5 has been discarded once, so it might be relatively safe.  \n\nConsidering hand improvement, keeping pairs (B2, B8, F2) and sequences (like B4-B5) is beneficial. Thus, discarding an isolated tile like W1 or W3 seems reasonable. Between them, W1 is a terminal, which is harder to use in chows (only pairs or pungs), and I have only one. W3 is also isolated. Since W3 is not a terminal, it might be slightly more flexible if I draw W2 or W4 later, but currently it's dead. I'll choose to discard W1 as it's a terminal with less utility.\n\nAnswer: Play W1"}
